# r7-server: DisplayPort. Already CONFIRMED hardware-impossible on this
# device - the USB-C port is USB 2.0-only with no DP Alt Mode lane support, so
# this can never do anything (see r7-usb2-only-no-dp-altmode).
# NOTE: CONFIG_EXYNOS_DISPLAYPORT is deliberately LEFT ON. Turning it off was
# tried and reverted: the DP driver is structurally entangled with the decon
# display core in this vendor tree - decon_reg.c, bts.c, decon.h and
# displayport.h all reference DP symbols WITHOUT a
# #if defined(CONFIG_EXYNOS_DISPLAYPORT) guard (only decon_core.c and
# decon_displayport.c are guarded). Disabling it therefore means patching the
# display driver itself, which is the one thing this device cannot afford to
# break - it is the console. Left compiled but inert instead: the USB-C port
# has no DP lanes (see r7-usb2-only-no-dp-altmode), so it can never probe or
# activate. Only its audio hook was cut, in include/sound/samsung/dp_ado.h.
# CONFIG_PHY_EXYNOS_DISPLAYPORT is not set
